meta {
  name: Node grain with no node
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/placements
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "curriculum_id": "{{curriculumId}}",
    "content_item_id": "{{libraryItemId}}",
    "grain": "node",
    "page_start": 12,
    "page_end": 28
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
}

docs {
  grain node promises a syllabus point and this body names none. Storing it
  would leave a row that claims to be precise and resolves to nothing: invisible
  to a node query because it has no node, and excluded from the curriculum-grain
  fallback because it says it is not one.

  The pair is guarded twice, at the API and by a check constraint on the table,
  because this is the shape a bulk import gets wrong and a constraint is the
  only guard a bulk import cannot go round.
}
